module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.receipt_names_a_property_not_the_tree_it_holds_of

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data receipt_names_a_property_not_the_tree_it_holds_of: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "receipt_names_a_property_not_the_tree_it_holds_of" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a receipt names a PROPERTY and never names the TREE it holds of, so it expires silently** (INVALID STATE: evidence of the form 'regenerating produces the committed bytes', 'the diff is zero', 'the census matches', 'the fixed point is reached' is a claim about A BASE, but is recorded and cited as a claim about A CHANGE. ",

    "When the base moves the receipt keeps reading as valid while describing a tree that no longer exists. ",

    "HARM: section 5 silent wrongness, and this is the WORST-SIGNALLING member of its family rather than merely another one -- a stale citation still shows the reader its text, an incompatible merge still conflicts, an absent observation still reports an absence; AN EXPIRED GREEN PRODUCES NOTHING AT ALL. ",

    "Nothing goes red, no conflict is raised, and the author's own careful re-verification re-affirms it, because re-running the same command against the same stale working tree reproduces the same true-of-nothing answer. ",

    "**DISTINCT FROM ITS TWO NEAREST NEIGHBOURS, and the repair law is what separates them.** `execution_provenance_loss` asks whether the observation RAN; here it ran and was valid, and then STOPPED being valid because its subject moved underneath it. ",

    "`positional_citation` is a decaying HANDLE -- a pointer that no longer names what it named; here the handle is fine and it is the EVIDENCE BINDING that decayed. ",

    "Different invalid states, different repairs. ",

    "**SPECIMEN (sunny-gull-270, PR #10036, 2026-09-02).** The PR's entire acceptance test was that the emitted .github/workflows/witnesses.yml is byte-identical after regeneration -- a behaviour-identical refactor whose whole claim is that the bytes do not move. ",

    "It was re-verified after each of three commits, and ALL THREE measurements were taken against a base main had already left: #10024 had landed and materially rewritten BOTH the authority the PR edits and the artifact under test -- re-derive the magnitudes with `git show --stat 7c310ed74c5 -- dag/gunbc/witness/witness_floor_workflow.dag .github/workflows/witnesses.yml`, which is an immutable commit and so answers the same forever. ",

    "No signal at any point. ",

    "The expiry was found by asking what had changed in main, not by any check. ",

    "**RECOGNITION RULE, mechanical: before citing a zero-diff or byte-identity receipt as merge evidence, ask whether the base moved ON THE FILES THE RECEIPT IS ABOUT** -- `git diff --stat $(git merge-base HEAD origin/main) origin/main -- <those paths>` -- because a receipt about generated bytes is invalidated only by changes to the authorities that produce them, and a whole-repository is-my-branch-behind check is both too coarse to act on and too noisy to keep. ",

    "**A SECOND, LESS OBVIOUS OBLIGATION: RE-DERIVE THE DISCRIMINATING CONTROL TOO, NOT ONLY THE RECEIPT.** A control taken before the merge proves the zero was readable on a tree that is not the one shipping, so a re-derived green beside a stale control is half a measurement. ",

    "And rebuild the PRODUCER: the tree and the emitter are two inputs, and a regeneration with one of them stale proves nothing about the pair. ",

    "**THE UPSIDE IS WORTH STATING BECAUSE IT CHANGES WHETHER PEOPLE DO IT: a receipt re-derived after a FOREIGN change to the same artifact is STRICTLY STRONGER than the original.** The first green only ever asks whether a projection reproduces its own base; the second asks whether it reproduces a base someone else moved -- which is where a projection that disagrees with the hand-kept form it replaced would actually surface. ",

    "**RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable.** Today the only defence is an author remembering to re-derive before citing, which is exactly the defence that does not survive a tired hour. ",

    "**CEILING: 2, mechanically preventable, and the reason it is not higher is that a receipt cannot make its subject stop moving -- what it can do is make the movement OBSERVABLE. ",

    "NEXT TRIGGER, named as the capability and not as an artifact: a receipt CARRIES THE BASE IT WAS MEASURED ON, so a producer can compare that base against HEAD and refuse an expired receipt, rather than a person remembering to. ",

    "THAT CAPABILITY IS NOT HYPOTHETICAL -- IT ALREADY EXISTS ONE SURFACE OVER, WHICH IS WHY THIS TRIGGER IS REACHABLE RATHER THAN ASPIRATIONAL: the review runner binds each review to the sha it was taken on and REFUSES on mismatch. ",

    "On this row's own pull request, review 58587 failed with `worktree freshness check failed: HEAD is ad388184ac but PR #10036 head is c80c9d88db -- refusing to review a stale/wrong checkout`, and a refused review is exactly the signal an expired receipt does not produce. ",

    "So reviews already carry their base and receipts do not; the gap is an UNAPPLIED mechanism rather than a missing one, and the trigger is discharged by giving regeneration receipts the binding reviews already have. ",

    "**THIS CITATION CARRIES ITS OWN BASE, because a row about receipts that expire must not carry one that has.** What is DURABLE is review 58587 itself: it is retrievable from the reviews API with status=failed, sha c80c9d88db and that error text, and a completed review is a historical fact that does not decay. ",

    "What is an OBSERVATION AT A TIME is the claim that the runner still behaves this way -- measured 2026-09-02, and NOT re-confirmed since, because the runner's source lives outside this repository and is not visible from a session container, so no gate here can check it and its absence from a local filesystem is not evidence either way. ",

    "Sampling later pull requests for a freshness failure -- `dashboard-ops reviews <pr>`, reading each review's status and error -- found none, and that is EXPECTED RATHER THAN REASSURING: the check fires only when a head moves mid-checkout, so a sample drawn where the condition did not arise discriminates nothing and no count of it is worth carrying. ",

    "**THAT UNCHECKABILITY IS ITSELF WHY THE TRIGGER NAMES A CAPABILITY AND NOT AN ARTIFACT** -- a trigger pointing at a file this repository cannot see would be satisfied or falsified by nothing observable here, which is the restoration-promise failure one row over. ",

    "Until that exists this row is the mitigation and citing it as coverage is rung inflation.**",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
